      "claim": "The commander is criminally responsible for the crimes even though the actual perpetrators were not members of the Military Police, because the crimes occurred within activities that were under the commander’s effective responsibility and control.",
      "reasoning": "Article 28(b) provides that a superior is liable for crimes committed by subordinates when \"the crimes concerned activities that were within the effective responsibility and control of the superior.\" The detention facilities were administered by the Military Police, which was under the commander’s authority; thus the environment in which the crimes occurred was within his effective responsibility. Customary rule 153 also imposes liability for failure to punish persons responsible, regardless of their formal affiliation.",
