    },
    {
      "claim": "The Trial Chamber proved each element of Article 7(3) of the ICTY Statute beyond reasonable doubt, satisfying the evidentiary threshold required for criminal conviction.",
      "reasoning": "The Chamber’s findings on effective control, knowledge (or constructive knowledge), and the failure to take all necessary and reasonable measures were based on a comprehensive record of documentary and testimonial evidence that was assessed and found to meet the \"beyond reasonable doubt\" standard, the highest standard of proof in international criminal trials. This standard is a well‑established principle of international criminal procedure.",
      "citations": []
